      "notes": "Codex works with my actual project files and terminal. Skills are reusable instructions, while Markdown keeps the goal and decisions visible. Git records changes, and worktrees keep separate experiments from mixing together. Pixi describes the software environment, and DataLad connects data and code with their history. When I need execution records, duct captures what a command did. These tools give the agent something concrete to act on, and give me something concrete to check. My skill workshop and worktree utilities are linked here.",
