      "notes": "Keyhatch tackles a very practical interruption: an agent needs a credential to do useful work. I'm building a native Mac app where I approve selected credentials once, then allow repeated retrieval during a limited window. Apple Passwords remains the source of truth, with selective import into Keyhatch. A local command-line client connects the agent to the broker. The important tradeoff is that a recipient can keep a disclosed secret. Expiry stops future retrieval; it cannot take that secret back. It's an experimental project with public source. Production signing and release validation remain unfinished.",
      "sources": [
        "https://github.com/leej3/keyhatch",
        "https://github.com/leej3/keyhatch/blob/main/SECURITY.md",
        "https://github.com/leej3/keyhatch/blob/main/docs/DISTRIBUTION.md"
      ]
    },
