        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "STAMPED principles",
          "x": 730,
          "y": 646,
          "w": 480,
          "h": 38,
          "size": 24,
          "bold": false,
          "color": "#15716e",
          "link": "https://stamped-principles.org/"
        }
      ],
      "notes": "The next talk asks, 'What did we just make?' A figure or report is only the visible result. The useful object also includes the inputs, code, decisions, and environment needed to inspect or rerun it. Our team's STAMPED principles give us a vocabulary: self-contained, tracked, actionable, modular, portable, ephemeral, and distributable. In plain terms: can I get the pieces, see their history, run the procedure, and recover a useful state elsewhere? This matters beyond science. An AI-generated website or spreadsheet also needs enough context for the next person.",
      "sources": [
        "https://research-object-with-ai.pages.dev/",
        "https://github.com/leej3/research-object-with-ai",
        "https://stamped-principles.org/"
      ]
    },
