      "notes": "Orinoco Lite is software I've been working on with agents. Research groups have information about people, projects, publications, and software scattered across many places. Here those become structured records with explicit relationships. The website and this graph are different views of those records. An editor proposes changes through GitHub, preserving a visible review history. It builds on upstream ORINOCO with a lighter Git-backed deployment. What interests me is shared context: people can browse it, software can validate it, and agents can work with a clearer description of what the group knows. This screenshot is saved, so the example works without Wi-Fi.",
      "sources": [
        "https://github.com/ORINOCO-Lite/orinoco-lite-dev",
        "https://dev.centerforopenneuroscience.org/explore/",
        "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22834595"
      ]
