      "notes": "The Zenodo record describes the original STAMPED in Practice proposal. The current poster PR captures the later public-data pilot, with working analyses and concrete failures to learn from. The next repository develops a repeated improvement process. Independent agents tackle the same scientific question under four kinds of assistance: baseline, general skill discovery, reproducibility-focused discovery, and explicit STAMPED skills. Independent judges assess scientific quality separately from how well the research object supports inspection and reuse. We then improve the skills and try again, keeping assessment fixed within a formal comparison. NARPS preparation pilots are already exposing useful problems. The hypothesis is that detailed STAMPED guidance improves performance and reduces inconsistent outcomes. The goal is transfer: a researcher brings their own data and hypothesis, and an independent agent can use these skills to do rigorous, convenient research. That improvement remains to be tested.",
      "sources": [
        "https://github.com/con/talks/pull/35",
        "https://zenodo.org/records/22833916",
        "https://github.com/leej3/stamped-ai-research-next",
        "https://github.com/leej3/stamped-ai-research-next/pull/3"
      ]
    },
